{"availability":"available","full":"jiupinjia/neural-magic-eye","name":"neural-magic-eye","description":"Neural Magic Eye: Learning to See and Understand the Scene Behind an Autostereogram, arXiv:2012.15692.","category":"Education","language":"Python","stars":81,"forks":13,"created":"2020-12-31T18:31:41Z","updated":"2021-01-07T01:23:29Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://jiupinjia.github.io/neuralmagiceye/","topics":[],"demo":"https://jiupinjia.github.io/neuralmagiceye/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-07T20:14:55.657Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-07T20:14:55.657Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-07T20:14:55.657Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-07T20:14:55.657Z","stars":81,"forks":13}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Official PyTorch implementation of the preprint paper \"NeuralMagicEye: Learning to See and Understand the Scene Behind an Autostereogram\", arXiv:2012.15692.","An autostereogram, a.k.a. magic eye image, is a single-image stereogram that can create visual illusions of 3D scenes from 2D textures. This paper studies an interesting question that whether a deep CNN can be trained to recover the depth behind an autostereogram and understand its content. The key to the autostereogram magic lies in the stereopsis - to solve such a problem, a model has to learn to discover and estimate disparity from the quasi-periodic textures. We show that deep CNNs embedded with disparity convolution, a novel convolutional layer proposed in this paper that simulates…","In this repository, we provide the complete training/inference implementation of our paper based on Pytorch and provide several demos that can be used for reproducing the results reported in our paper. With the code, you can also try on your own data by following the instructions below."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/jiupinjia/neural-magic-eye/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"3961ab1d41166ecbb76ef1956261b22866a